Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[TextData[StyleBox["pmx (predict molecular cross sections)",
 FontWeight->"Bold"]], "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.875922571008416*^9, 3.875922626363906*^9}, 
   3.8833288049909973`*^9, {3.9009341111373243`*^9, 3.9009341351727605`*^9}, {
   3.9026996313492093`*^9, 3.9026996438471603`*^9}},
 FontWeight->"Plain",ExpressionUUID->"732f5231-02ac-4b63-bf5c-ad96d4aff4e7"],

Cell["A. L. Harris and J. Nepomuceno", "Subtitle",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9009341405889883`*^9, 3.9009341550944085`*^9}, {
  3.9026996230987835`*^9, 
  3.902699627813285*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8681ccfd-0848-466f-9625-\
baa84ebf8d6b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This Mathematica code was used to produce the data published in \n\
https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2309.02538.  ",
 StyleBox["Please cite this code as:   A. L. Harris and J. Nepomuceno, doi: \
10.6084/m9.figshare.24082035  and  \t\n\
https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2309.02538\n",
  FontSize->16,
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\nThe program reads experimental data for total ionization cross sections \
of molecular targets, trains a 3-layer neural network, and makes predictions \
for molecular targets not in the training set. \n\nThe network inputs are: \
number of atoms in a molecule, ionization potential\nThe network outputs are: \
ionization cross section at preset grid of 101 incident projectile energies\n\
\nExperimental datasets used for training are stored in the directory \
Mathematica.data/input/converted_interped.  This directory should be located \
in the working directory of this code.  Also in this directory is a file that \
contains a list of the data file names, \[OpenCurlyQuote]converted_files.txt\
\[CloseCurlyQuote].\n\nThe user parameters in this code are as follows and \
are set at various points throughout the code.  They can be found by \
searching for \[OpenCurlyQuote]user supplied\[CloseCurlyQuote].\nnmols\n\
nepochs\ntrialnum\n\nResults will be placed into a session directory and \
trial directory.  The user supplies the session number interactively when the \
program is executed.  The trial number is set by the user in the code - \
search \[OpenCurlyQuote]user supplied\[CloseCurlyQuote].\n\nFor repeated \
trials with the same molecule sets in training/testing, after the first \
trial, it is sufficient to only run the \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Training/testing section\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] cell. \
 If configuration changes to the molecular training sets are made, then the \
program needs to run from the beginning.\n\nOutput files are:\n  In the Trial \
Directory: \n    biases_layer_1.csv (biases for connections between input \
layer and hidden layer)\n    biases_layer2.csv (biases for connections \
between hidden layer and output layer)\n    [testing molecule output].csv \
(predictions for the testing molecule.  columns in data file are energy (eV) \
and cross section (a0^2)\n    input_molecules.csv (list of molecules used in \
training)\n    network.png (screen capture of loss function during training)\n\
    weights_layer_1.csv (weights for connections between input layer and \
hidden layer)\n    weights_layer_2.csv (weights for connections between \
hidden layer and output layer)\n  In the figs directory: \n    [testing \
molecule output].png (comparison of algorithm prediction and known \
experimental data)\n    weights_layer1_2.png (matrix plot of weights for \
connections between input layer and hidden layer)\n    weights_layer2_3.png \
(matrix plot of weights for connections between hidden layer and output \
layer)\n"
}], "Text",
